==Latvian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|lv|orv|умъ||mind, intellect}} ([[cf]]. {{cog|ru|ум||mind, intellect, wit}}), cognate with {{cog|lt|aumuõ||understanding, notion, intellect}}, [[genitive]] {{m|lt|aumeñs}}. This word was borrowed into Latvian before the 13th century, while {{cog|orv|-}} ''у'' was still close to [o] in pronunciation. It conserved its original meaning (“mind,” “understanding”) well into the 19th century; the modern sense was an innovation introduced by {{coin|notext=1|lv|Atis Kronvalds}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|uōma|level}}
{{rfap|lv}}

===Noun===
